[29.611893, "o", "  ⚙ bash ls /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ | head -30 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 9 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip* 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip* 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Found the problem. The `pip` directory (the actual Python package code) i…\r\n  │ Let me fix this by bootstrapping pip properly.\r\n[approval] bash: rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash "]
[29.611989, "o", "— exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 13 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 14 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me verify it actually works by doing a dry-run install:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run requests 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚠ .gnomon/roles.toml [roles.verifier]: the completion reviewer is run read-only, so note is withheld from it during a review.\r\nFixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Problem:** The `pip` Python package files were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`. Only the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory remained — the actual `pip/` source code directory was gone. The `pip3` binary in `/usr/local/bin/` was still there and pointed to the missing module, causing `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.\r\n\r\n**F"]
[29.612012, "o", "ix:** Removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory and reinstalled pip cleanly using `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which restored the full pip package.\r\n\r\n`pip3` and `python3 -m pip` both work correctly now.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=15 surface=e9a3788f4265\r\n"]
